# =============================================================================
# .env — SECRETS AND API CREDENTIALS ONLY (copy to .env; file is gitignored)
# =============================================================================
#
# Do NOT use this file for training, inference, or WASM runtime configuration.
# Put those in versioned TOML and the Training WUI:
#   - Training:  configs/training/*.toml  (see configs/training/schema.toml)
#   - WUI:       training-wui/README.md
#   - Serve:     configs/serve/*.toml
#
# python-dotenv loads .env for processes that need tokens (engine, uvicorn, WUI).
#
# CI, Docker, serverless, and local dev may still inject other variables; see:
#   docs/ENV_CI_OVERRIDES.md
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Hugging Face Hub (optional: gated datasets, rate limits)
# Raw token only — no extra quotes or braces.
# HUGGING_FACE_HUB_TOKEN=hf_...
# HF_TOKEN=

# --- IBM Quantum (optional; Qiskit IBM Runtime — see docs/QUANTUM_QISKIT.md)
# IBM_QUANTUM_API_TOKEN=
# QISKIT_IBM_TOKEN=
# Backend selection belongs in training TOML [hardware].quantum_backend / wizard.

# --- RunPod (optional) — see docs/RUNPOD_QUICKSTART.md, docs/RUNPOD_SERVERLESS.md
# RUNPOD_TOKEN=
# RUNPOD_API_KEY=
# RUNPOD_TOKEN_END=
# RUNPOD_SERVERLESS_ENDPOINT_ID=
# SSH paths for remote training are deployment details; prefer WUI / warm-target registry where possible.
# RUNPOD_SSH_USER=root
# RUNPOD_REMOTE_DIR=/workspace/qminiwasm-core
# RUNPOD_SSH_KEY=C:\Users\you\.ssh\id_ed25519
